From ede16659ba01de834442c77ba1fe7d64a079c5ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max rossi <113717219+maxr0ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:05:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] d3dx9: Rerun only the preshader instructions whose inputs
 changed.

A preshader that never reads a temporary or output register before writing
it in the same run is a pure function of its constant input table. Keep a
copy of that table as of the last run: when no input register changed, the
outputs left in the register tables are exactly what a run would compute and
the run is skipped; otherwise only the instructions that depend on a changed
register run, together with the writers of the values they read (a skipped
writer's register may have been reused since) and the last writer of every
output component one of them writes. The rest of the outputs keep the values
the last run computed from the same inputs.

RotWK sets the camera, lights and fog again for every batch and the per-object
parameters for every mesh, mostly to the values they already had, so most
preshader runs become no-ops or a handful of instructions.

Not used for preshaders with relative addressing outside the constant table,
vertex inputs (tx_1), instructions that fail, or outputs sharing registers with
constants set from parameters. Clear bit 0x2 of WINE_D3DX9_FXOPT to turn it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
